  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "The Gateway And Query Planning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Plan Caching"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cache keys on the normalized operation text",
            "Cold plans on large schemas cost tens of milliseconds",
            "Persisted queries and safelisting let the router pre-plan",
            "Then each request skips parsing and planning outright"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How A Plan Unfolds"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Step 1 hits an entry-point subgraph owning a root field",
            "Later steps send `_entities` with reps pulled by `Flatten`",
            "Sibling branches with no data dependency plan as `Parallel`",
            "`@requires` forces those steps into a `Sequence`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Fetch entry",
              "Flatten path",
              "_entities fetch",
              "stitch shape"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Response is restitched into the client's requested shape",
            "`__typename` is injected automatically to route entities",
            "Clients never see the join machinery"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Runtime Facts"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Apollo Router (Rust) replaced Node `@apollo/gateway`",
            "Same planning semantics, far lower per-request overhead",
            "Router owns auth headers, rate limits, APQ, caching, telemetry",
            "No retry of subgraph errors: `errors` plus `null` in `data`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Reading Plans In Dev",
          "items": [
            "`?dry-run` returns the plan without executing",
            "`query-planner` trace in Apollo Explorer",
            "`ApolloServerPluginInlineTrace` per subgraph"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Latency Suspect One",
          "text": "Deep fetch chains are the number one federation latency bug. Read the query plan before you blame the database."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Models",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Stitching",
                "lines": [
                  "Hand-written merge config",
                  "`delegateToSchema` calls",
                  "Gateway holds join logic"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Federation",
                "lines": [
                  "Subgraphs declare directives",
                  "Gateway derives routing",
                  "Composition proves it"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Federation vs Schema Stitching",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Dimension",
            "Stitching",
            "Federation"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "join logic",
              "central gateway",
              "in the services"
            ],
            [
              "new cross field",
              "edit gateway repo",
              "edit subgraph, republish"
            ],
            [
              "deploy",
              "gateway redeploy",
              "router hot-reload"
            ],
            [
              "conflicts",
              "rename/transform",
              "composition rejects build"
            ],
            [
              "mistakes appear",
              "at runtime",
              "at composition time"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// stitching: logic lives in gateway code",
            "resolve: (_, args, ctx, info) =>",
            "  delegateToSchema({ schema: users, info })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Non-GraphQL Sources"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stitching and Mesh wrap REST, gRPC, OpenAPI easily",
            "Federation needs a subgraph shim in front of each",
            "That shim is code you must own and operate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Cannot touch the upstream server?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "You cannot add `@key` to someone else's schema",
            "Stitching wins outright for legacy and third-party",
            "Or wrap it in a thin subgraph shim you do control"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ecosystem And Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stitching lives in `@graphql-tools`, no registry required",
            "Federation: Apollo, Cosmo, Hive, and Mesh speaks both",
            "Federation demands composition build infrastructure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking One"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stitch: few schemas, no subgraph control, mixed backends",
            "Federate: many teams, real ownership, compile-time guarantees",
            "Team count decides this more often than technology does"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Not Exclusive",
          "text": "GraphQL Mesh can present stitched REST and gRPC sources as a federated subgraph. Combine the two instead of choosing sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Latency Bill",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A query chaining 3 subgraphs costs 3 serial round trips",
            "N+1 crosses the boundary: 100 products, 100 reviews fetches",
            "Only `_entities` batching plus DataLoader avoids it",
            "Client sees one request; you paid for three"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs And Failure Modes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When A Subgraph Dies"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{ \"data\": { \"me\": { \"reviews\": null } },",
            "  \"errors\": [{ \"path\": [\"me\",\"reviews\"],",
            "    \"message\": \"reviews subgraph 500\" }] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One subgraph 500s: valid `data` with null holes plus `errors`",
            "A failing non-null field nulls the nearest nullable ancestor",
            "Nullability is your blast radius — design it deliberately",
            "Timeouts and circuit breaking belong in the router"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Trust Nothing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Router forwards headers; each subgraph authorizes on its own",
            "Never treat gateway-side auth as sufficient",
            "Propagate identity explicitly, do not assume shared context",
            "Cost and depth limits run at the router, before planning"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cache",
            "Problem it solves"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "APQ",
              "request payload size"
            ],
            [
              "query plan cache",
              "planning CPU cost"
            ],
            [
              "entity cache",
              "subgraph fetch cost"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "OpenTelemetry tracing is non-optional here",
            "One client query becomes N spans across N services",
            "Without it, a slow query has no owner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shapes That Go Wrong"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "God subgraph owning most entities: the monolith plus a hop",
            "Chatty chaining A to B to C back to A",
            "Splitting by technical layer, not by business domain"
          ]
        },
        {
